    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436-a4">

                <pb facs="0764" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg694"/>

                <head>Mr. Dickinson to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 17, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit to you a translation of a note
                    which I have received from the minister for foreign affairs of this government,
                    showing that certain agents of the British government are disposed to revive
                    their old protectorate over the Mosquito coast, which Nicaragua regards as an
                    infringement upon her sovereignty.</p>
                <p>I also transmit the same to the Department of State at Washington.</p>
                <p>Should you be able, by your good offices, to contribute in any manner towards a
                    settlement of this vexed question between the two countries, you would be not
                    only preventing much future trouble, but acting, as it seems to me, in
                    accordance with the uniform policy of our government.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. B. DICKINSON.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., London.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
